Hi Richard

Sorry for this again. The model worked well, but now I would like to include the covariates that I am actually interested in (winter and summer temperatures). So, I wanted to see how temperature affect the abundance of these birds so I want to use is in yearlySiteCovs (oc1), but I get an error message and I do not understand why...

sc1<-reshape(subset(anapla.dat,select=c("Year","Site", "Habitat", "Whole")),     # SiteCovs

             timevar = "Year",idvar = "Site",direction="wide")

oc1<-reshape(subset(anapla.dat,select=c("Year","Site","Whole", "Boat","Scope","SummerTemp", "WinterTemp")),   # yearlySiteCovs

             timevar = "Year",idvar = "Site", direction="wide")

boat <- oc1[,paste("Boat", 1986:2014, sep=".")]
scope <- oc1[,paste("Scope", 1986:2014, sep=".")]
habitat <- sc1[,paste("Habitat", 1986:2014, sep=".")]
whole <- sc1[,paste("Whole", 1986:2014, sep=".")]

summerTemp <- oc1[,paste("SummerTemp", 1986:2014, sep=".")]
winterTemp <- oc1[,paste("WinterTemp", 1986:2014, sep=".")]

um.dat.covs<- unmarkedFramePCO(y = y[,2:30],

                               siteCovs = sc1[,c("Habitat.1986", "Whole.1986")] ,                                         # This is only for the spatial variation in initial abundance.
                               yearlySiteCovs=list(boat=boat, scope=scope, whole=whole, habitat=habitat,
                                                   summerTemp=summerTemp, winterTemp=winterTemp),              # This is for the spatio-temporal variation in abundance after year 1
                               numPrimary=T)

Error in checkAtAssignment("unmarkedMultFrame", "numPrimary", "logical") :
  assignment of an object of class “logical” is not valid for @‘numPrimary’ in an object of class “unmarkedMultFrame”; is(value, "numeric") is not TRUE

Thank you very much.

Best

Diego

El martes, 31 de marzo de 2015, 15:48:58 (UTC+3), Richard Chandler escribió:
> Hi Diego,
>
> There are 3 processes that you can model with pcountOpen: (1) spatial variation in initial abundance, (2) spatio-temporal variation in abundance after year 1, and (3) detection conditional on abundance. If you want to model the effect of habitat and whole on all years, then you need model both initial abundance using siteCovs and subsequent abundance using yearlySiteCovs. You only need obsCovs if you have robust design data.
>
> Richard
>
>
