Hi Diego, you've set numPrimary=T and unless T has been defined as a number somewhere in your workspace, R will read it as TRUE.  That error message is saying that numPrimary has been specified as an object of class "logical", which is what TRUE and FALSE are.  Make sure you either define T as an integer or assign that integer directly to numPrimary in your call to create the umf.

